###########################################################################
# Positive fixture for the SSTIM Kernel Profile.
#
# The Kernel owns two classes and nothing else: sstim:Stimulation and its
# sensory specialisation. This graph is therefore deliberately almost empty —
# any additional SSTIM predicate would come from a module Kernel does not
# import, and the point of the fixture is that the anchor is usable alone.
#
# Kernel declares no shape closure, so this fixture is not validated: it is
# executed by the Kernel competency query (ADR 0045). Both types are asserted
# explicitly because every profile declares inference mode "none", so nothing
# derives Stimulation from SensoryStimulation at query time.
###########################################################################

@prefix example: <https://example.org/sstim/kernel-fixture/> .
@prefix sstim:   <https://w3id.org/sstim#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

example:process a sstim:Stimulation, sstim:SensoryStimulation ;
    rdfs:label "A sensory stimulation process"@en .
